  "body": "## \ud83c\udfaf Changes\n\n`test:types` for `examples/vue/algolia` fails with `TS2589: Type instantiation is excessively deep and possibly infinite.` at the `useInfiniteQuery` call in `SearchResults.vue` once `@tanstack/vue-query` is built from current `main`.\n\n`SearchResponse.hits` was typed as Algolia's `Hit<TData>`, which includes recursive highlight types. The example only reads `objectID` and the `Product` fields, so `hits` is now typed as `Array<TData & { objectID: string }>` and the `@algolia/client-search` type import is removed.\n\n## \u2705 Checklist\n\n- [x] I have followed the steps in the [Contributing guide](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md).\n- [x] I have tested code changes locally with `pnpm run test:pr`, or these tests do not apply to this pull request.\n- [x] I have followed the [AI contribution policy](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/AI_POLICY.md) and fully understand the code in this pull request, including any code generated with AI assistance.\n\n## \ud83d\ude80 Release Impact\n\n- [ ] This change affects published code, and I have generated a [changeset](https://github.com/changesets/changesets/blob/main/docs/adding-a-changeset.md).\n- [x] This change is docs/CI/dev-only (no release).\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n<!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n- **Improvements**\n  - Product search results now expose each result\u2019s identifier directly alongside its data, making the result shape clearer for developers. This is a typing-only update; it does not change the search experience or how results are returned at runtime.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->",
